Z||000004||Bazooka||05-27-2001||04:44 PM||||'The Fast And The Furious' sounds like a new approach to draw in the 'street racer' crowd to the cinema. With summer coming up and Drag Racing coming into its most popular season, Its rare to see a wheelstander on the street but occassionally there is someone that will risk his hard work for the spectacle. Also, too bad there isn't much of a Fiero market for wheelstanding. I've personally seen only 2 Fiero photos that were pulling wheelies at the strip over the years. Very tough to accomplish. Fast cars like Pat Ciarcia (10 second 1/4 miles) are one thing, but lifting the front wheels up is another. Tire Characteristics, Gearing, Horsepower, and Weight Distribution are factors that do not favor the Fiero. Still, this movie sounds entertaining and may be the best thing going since Steve McQueen. SEE IT! <BR>  <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> <BR> <BR>**********************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Taijiguy:<BR><B>Anyone else seen the ads for this flick? Hot Holy Mother of Mud! I just saw it (during the Indy 500) It's about street racing, showed a quick clip of an old Barracuda flat out pulling a wheelstand at a stop light. Good Lord I can't wait for this one to hit the theaters! Can only imagine what the sound will be like in a movie theater! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>**************************************<BR>||||reg||1
