Z||000014||Cheever2||05-27-2001||07:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cameron:<BR>Pearl Harbor.  That should be a good movie. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I saw that one yesterday.  Figgered since the critics didn't like it then it MUST be good.  And my opinion was that it was great.  It spent too much time on the fictional love story, and had way too many close-ups on pretty-boy Ben Affleck (did you just see a duck somewhere?), but the action scenes left me totally amazed.  I'm still tryng to come up with words that explain how outstanding the action sequences were.<P>You GOTTA see Pearl Harbor on the BIG SCREEN.  I'm going to see it again before it leaves the theaters.  Of course, I'm still a kid who wants to fly fighter planes when I grow up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||cadaver||05-28-2001||12:21 AM||||Back when I was running on the street. It was not that uncommon to see trailered cars. Pulling the front wheels for a block. I was out one night night and this guy pulls up with a covered trailer. Next thing you know he is rolling of a needle nose drag car. Not like you see on the strip. It was short with the engine in the front. Like the 60's-70's dragsters. That lite up the night like nothing else. Lost to a camaro. Then it was "Hurry load them up and leave" ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Nashco||05-28-2001||04:58 AM||||Seeing that CHARGER (I recognized it in a second, I love them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) get demolished in the preview kind of turned me off.  Seems the sport compact crowd is starting to think a little much of themselves.  I love a small car as much/more than anybody here...that's all I own; but a 69 Charger with probably a 440 and a blower on it would basically annihilate anything on the road in a straight line.<P>I can't wait to see the movie to see how they treat the race with the Charger....I'm hoping they just came around a corner and the Charger lost control.  That would be a bragging point of the compact cars...and wouldn't put the Charger to shame.  The old muscle cars just weren't built for cornering, they didn't care back then for the most part.  Now, if they show the Charger just wasn't fast enough to get ahead of the compact car and get in front of him, I'll be really pissed.<P>Like I said, I am afraid this movie will spurn more 15-25 year old idiots into thinking a compact car can do anything.  I am 19, with a fair knowledge about cars, if I do say so myself.  I hate the "my car is lowered, so it must be fast" attitude that a lot of the (for lack of a better term) ricers have.  The term ricer seems to be changing meaning nowadays...instead of a Japanese car, it's now connotating a car with no real performance value, but a car searching to obtain a look.<P>Anyway, I downloaded the high-definition 60 second preview about five months ago...and it evoked some major emotions from me; everytime I watch it that ending pisses me off.  I do like watching the Honda go under the semi though...I hope to do that someday <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I can't wait to see that movie in the theaters.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
